id: pm-gh1657
title: "GH-1657: release notes mark SDK contract changes with a migration line instead of shipping them under Fixed"
description: "Between 2026.10.25 and 2026.10.30 seven changes altered observable SDK behaviour (GH-1554, GH-1577 pm-gh1577, GH-1583, GH-1591 pm-pllp78, GH-1613, GH-1614 pm-gh1614, GH-1617). Six shipped under Fixed and one under Security, none with a migration line, and one Dependabot bump broke 9 of 34 downstream extensions. pm-cli side: a way to declare an item a contract change with a before/after/migrate line, and a release check that requires that declaration when the public SDK surface snapshot or a documented default changes. pm-changelog side (fix in the pm-changelog repo, not here): render a Changed (SDK contract) section from that declaration, and expose it in changelog JSON for fleets."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: changelog,ecosystem,"gh:1657",release,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-03T21:20:20.562Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T02:22:41.233Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "A closed item can declare an observable SDK or CLI contract change as a complete contract line (before, after and migrate, all three required) through existing pm metadata, documented in docs/RELEASING.md; pm-changelog renders each declared contract change under a Changed (SDK contract) section as before, after and migrate, and refuses or flags a declaration missing any part; tracked and fixed in the pm-changelog repo (unbraind/pm-changelog#317); A release-time check refuses an Unreleased window whose public SDK surface snapshot (sdk/public-surface.json) or a documented default (the defaults tables in docs/CONFIGURATION.md and docs/SDK.md) changed without any declared contract change"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: A release that changes an observable SDK or CLI contract lists that change with a before/after/migrate line under a Changed (SDK contract) section
actual_result: Contract changes ship under Fixed or Security with no migration line; one toolchain bump broke 9 of 34 downstream extensions
